  "feesApplyText": "Tenancy Information:\nBefore Your Tenancy Begins\n\nHolding Deposit\nOnce your offer has been accepted, a holding deposit equivalent to one week's rent is payable. This amount will be credited toward your advance rent if you successfully enter into a tenancy agreement.\n\nAdvance Rent\nRent is payable in advance for each tenancy. At a minimum, the first month's rent must be paid prior to the tenancy start date. The exact amount may vary depending on the specific terms of your agreement.\n\nTenancy Deposit\nA security deposit is payable before the tenancy begins:\n-\t5 weeks' rent (if annual rent is under \u00a350,000)\n-\t6 weeks' rent (if annual rent is \u00a350,000 or more)\n\nLate Payment of Rent\nInterest on late rent payments will be charged at 3% above the Bank of England's base lending rate. This charge will only apply if the rent is more than 14 days overdue.\n\nContract Changes\nShould you request a variation, novation, or amendment to the tenancy agreement (including a change of occupant), an administration fee of \u00a350 (inc. VAT) will apply. All changes are subject to the landlord's approval.\n\nEarly Termination\nIf you wish to end your tenancy before the agreed term, you will be responsible for:\n-\tThe landlord's costs in re-letting the property\n-\tRent, council tax, and utilities until a new tenancy begins or until the original tenancy expires\n-\tWhichever occurs first, the costs will not exceed the total remaining rent owed under the original agreement.\n\nVacating During Tenancy\nShould you vacate the property before the end of the term, you remain liable for all rent and associated payments until either:\n-\tThe end of the tenancy term\n-\tA new tenancy commences with a suitable replacement tenant.\n-\tWhichever occurs first, regardless of whether you continue to occupy the property.\n\n________________________________________\n\nAdditional Information\n-\tTilson & Spencer is a member of SafeAgent\n-\tTilson & Spencer is part of the SafeAgent Client Money Protection Scheme\n-\tTilson & Spencer is a member of The Property Ombudsman Scheme\n",
